Inclusions: They call me the Seeker
Inclusions: You can't tell me what I am living for

Body:

Unlike most species of life, our human natures are not determined primarily by genetics. That is, our behaviors are not hardwired into our genes. Instead, our genes prepare us to learn and adapt, not primarily through genetic evolution, but through cultural evolution. In other words, we discover new things, and then share that knowledge with others. It is this ability that has made up the most adaptive species on the planet. 

But it is also this lack of a definite identity that sets us on a quest to find out just who we are, and why we are here. 

